IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hta-offences`

-- Hostage-Taking Act 2010, ss 2 to 12 and 14(1) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_hostage-taking-act-2010.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`hijackers demanding a prisoner release` MEANS Incident WITH
    `A seized or detained B` IS TRUE
    `A threatened death, hurt or continued detention` IS TRUE
    `A's conduct gave a reasonable apprehension of death, hurt or continued detention` IS FALSE
    `A caused death or hurt to B` IS FALSE
    `to compel a government or intergovernmental organisation` IS TRUE
    `to compel any other person` IS FALSE
    `an offence under s 3 of the Geneva Conventions Act 1973` IS FALSE

`kidnappers demanding ransom from a family` MEANS Incident WITH
